Spec: Course entity and courses page

Purpose:
  The Course entity: a unique name, a description and an ECTS credit count, and the admin page that lists Courses
  and creates, edits or removes them. Because a Course is taught through ../realizations/realizations.sdd's
  CourseRealizations, this page also lists each Course's realizations, is where the admin adds, edits or removes one,
  and where a Course's removal cascades to its realizations and their Lessons. The weekly calendar is
  per-CourseRealization and lives in ../realizations/realizations.sdd, which reads Courses through ./services.py to
  compose its display label.

Owns:
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py
  ./view.py
  ./routes.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../auth/auth.sdd
  ../semester/semester.sdd
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd
  ../lessons/lessons.sdd

Must:
  A Course has a unique name, a description and an ECTS credit count.
  @CourseService.add_course rejects an empty name with @InvalidCourseError and a name matching an existing
    Course's (ignoring surrounding whitespace and letter case) with @DuplicateCourseError, before storage.
  @CourseService.update_course applies the same name checks, ignores the Course being edited when looking for a
    duplicate, and rejects an unknown id with @UnknownCourseError before storage.
  @CourseService.delete_course rejects an unknown id with @UnknownCourseError before storage.
  No color is stored on a Course; ../semester/semester.sdd's view assigns display colors dynamically per
    CourseRealization.
  @CourseRepository in ./ports.py exposes list, get, add, update and delete operations backing ./services.py.
  ./routes.py registers the courses page at `/courses`, shown as the Courses tab between Semester and Realizations
    in ../shared/shared.sdd's nav.
  The courses page shows ../shared/shared.sdd's persistent Semester selector with every Semester from
    ../semester/semester.sdd's @SemesterService; the selection does not filter the page because Courses are not
    scoped to a Semester, and it only prefills the Semester select of the add-realization `<dialog>`.
  When no Courses exist, the page shows the create-Course form as its primary content to an admin session, and a
    neutral notice to a visitor.
  When Courses exist, the page lists every Course with its name, description and ECTS credits.
  Every listed Course also lists its ../realizations/realizations.sdd realizations across every Semester, each with
    its group and Semester label and a link to that realization's weekly view.
  For the admin, clicking a listed Course opens a `<dialog>` modal whose form is prefilled with that Course's
    values and submitting it updates the Course; the admin-only `+ New Course` control links to `GET /courses/new`,
    which renders the same create form. That dialog also carries a `Delete Course` control opening a
    confirmation `<dialog>` that names the Course and, when it has any, how many of its realizations and Lessons the
    removal takes with it; submitting it posts to `/courses/{course_id}/delete`, which removes the Course's
    realizations with their Lessons before the Course itself, and re-renders a validation message when the Course is
    unknown.
  For the admin, a `+ Add Realization` control on each listed Course opens a `<dialog>` modal whose form takes a
    group label and a Semester, posts to `/courses/{course_id}/realizations` and creates the realization through
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's @RealizationService; that route is rejected by ../auth/auth.sdd's guard for
    non-admin sessions, and its validation errors are re-rendered as a validation message on this page.
  For the admin, each listed realization carries an `Edit` control opening a `<dialog>` prefilled with that
    realization's group and Semester, posting to `/courses/{course_id}/realizations/{realization_id}` and updating it
    through ../realizations/realizations.sdd's @RealizationService, which keeps the realization's Course, and a
    `Delete` control opening a confirmation `<dialog>` that names how many Lessons go with it before posting to
    `/courses/{course_id}/realizations/{realization_id}/delete`; deleting one leaves the Course itself untouched.
  When no Semester exists, the add-realization and edit-realization `<dialog>`s report that instead of offering a
    Semester select that cannot be filled.
  Course and realization write routes, including the deletions, are rejected by ../auth/auth.sdd's guard for
    non-admin sessions and re-render a validation message when the name is empty or already used, when the Semester
    or the entry is unknown.
  Visitors see the Course list and each Course's realizations without editing or deleting affordances.
  ./view.py and ./routes.py read ../realizations/realizations.sdd only through its services.py, never its domain.py
    or repository_sqlite.py, so this pair is the mutual dependency ../architecture.sdd permits.

Done when:
  Every scenario has a test.

Scenario: Admin creates the first Course
  Given no Courses exist
  And the admin is logged in
  When the admin opens the courses page and submits a name, a description and an ECTS credit count
  Then the courses page lists the new Course

Scenario: Visitor sees the empty courses page
  Given no Courses exist
  And the visitor is not logged in
  When the visitor opens the courses page
  Then the page shows a neutral notice and no create form

Scenario: Admin edits a Course
  Given a Course exists
  And the admin is logged in
  When the admin clicks the Course, changes its values in the dialog and submits
  Then the courses page lists the updated Course

Scenario: Editing to a duplicate name is rejected
  Given two Courses exist
  When the admin renames one to the other's name
  Then the update is rejected with a validation message

Scenario: Admin adds a realization to a Course
  Given a Course and a Semester exist
  And the admin is logged in
  When the admin opens that Course's add-realization dialog and submits a group label and the Semester
  Then the Course lists the new realization with its group and Semester, linking to its weekly view

Scenario: Visitor sees a Course's realizations
  Given a Course has a realization
  And the visitor is not logged in
  When the visitor opens the courses page
  Then the Course lists its realization and no add-realization control

Scenario: Adding a realization without a Semester is refused
  Given no Semester exists
  When the admin opens a Course's add-realization dialog
  Then the dialog reports that no Semester exists instead of offering a Semester select

Scenario: Admin deletes a Course
  Given a Course with two realizations exists, one of them with Lessons
  And the admin is logged in
  When the admin confirms the Course's delete dialog, which names the realizations and Lessons it removes
  Then the courses page no longer lists the Course, its realizations or their Lessons

Scenario: Admin deletes a realization
  Given a Course has a realization with Lessons
  And the admin is logged in
  When the admin confirms that realization's delete dialog, which names its Lessons
  Then the Course no longer lists the realization and the realization has no Lessons

Scenario: Admin edits a realization
  Given a Course has a realization
  And the admin is logged in
  When the admin changes the realization's group and Semester in its edit dialog and submits
  Then the Course lists the realization with the new group and Semester label

Scenario: Visitor sees no editing or deleting affordances
  Given a Course with a realization exists
  And the visitor is not logged in
  When the visitor opens the courses page
  Then no dialog or edit or delete control is shown for the Course or its realization

Tasks:
  [x] Implement @Course in ./domain.py and a hardcoded ./services.py returning two placeholder Courses, standing in
    for @CourseRepository until persistence exists
  [x] Replace the hardcoded ./services.py with a class-based @CourseRepository-backed `CourseService` (./ports.py
    and ./repository_sqlite.py), per ../architecture.sdd's Example
  [x] Enforce unique, non-empty Course names in @CourseService.add_course with @InvalidCourseError and
    @DuplicateCourseError
  [x] Add the courses page in ./view.py and ./routes.py: create form when no Courses exist, Course list with the
    admin-only `+ New Course` control and edit `<dialog>`, and @CourseService.update_course with @UnknownCourseError
  [x] List each Course's ../realizations/realizations.sdd realizations in ./view.py, read through that package's
    services.py in ./routes.py, each linking to its weekly view
  [x] Add the admin-only `+ Add Realization` control and its `<dialog>` to ./view.py, and the guarded
    `POST /courses/{course_id}/realizations` route in ./routes.py that creates one through
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's @RealizationService
  [x] Add a per-Course delete `<dialog>` naming the realizations and Lessons the cascade removes, @CourseService.delete_course
    and the guarded `POST /courses/{course_id}/delete` route that removes the realizations with their Lessons first
  [x] Add a per-realization edit `<dialog>` and a delete `<dialog>` naming the Lessons it removes to ./view.py, and
    the guarded update and delete routes in ./routes.py that write through ../realizations/realizations.sdd's
    @RealizationService
